# Daintree Assistant — example environment.
#
# The CLI holds NO model-provider credential and has no provider client. Every model
# call goes: CLI ──▶ Daintree Assistant backend ──▶ the upstream provider ──▶ the model.
# The backend owns prompt assembly, runbook selection, model choice, AND the upstream key:
# a request from the CLI carries no Authorization header at all, and Daintree pays. There
# is no provider API key in this process.
#
# ── Nothing in this file is required. ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no sign-in and nothing to configure to get started — the binary works as soon
# as it is on your PATH. Everything below is an override for development.

# ── Trust boundary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings resolve as: CLI flags > real process env (snapshotted BEFORE any .env loads)
# > the bound project's .env > the assistant's own .env > built-in defaults. Three tiers
# decide which of those sources a given setting may come from:
#
#   trusted-only   real process env / CLI flags ONLY. A bound repo must never be able to
#                  escalate the assistant, redirect where a turn is sent, or supply a
#                  spendable bearer on your behalf.
#                  → DAINTREE_API_KEY, DAINTREE_BACKEND_URL, DAINTREE_ALLOW_INSECURE_BACKEND,
#                    DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_TIER, DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_AUTO_APPROVE,
#                    DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_OFFLINE, DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_STATE_DIR,
#                    DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_LOG_DIR
#   trusted-or-own real env or THIS repo's .env, never the bound project's.
#                  → DAINTREE_MCP_URL, DAINTREE_MCP_TOKEN, DAINTREE_PROJECT_ID,
#                    DAINTREE_WINDOW_ID, DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_DEBUG_LOG,
#                    DAINTREE_WORKFLOW_INTELLIGENCE
#   merged         everything else: real env > project .env > own .env.
#
# So: putting DAINTREE_API_KEY in a project's .env does nothing. That is deliberate.

# ── Backend endpoint (trusted env only) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The URL override IS the local dev loop — point it at a backend you are running.
# Deployed (default): https://assistant.daintree.org
# Local backend:      cd ../assistant-backend && python -m daintree_assistant_server
# DAINTREE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8473
#
# A REMOTE (non-loopback) endpoint must be https:// — a turn's conversation, terminal
# output, file excerpts and tool results all cross that wire, with or without a bearer.
# Loopback (above) is always exempt. Set this only if you deliberately want a plaintext
# remote endpoint and understand the risk.
# DAINTREE_ALLOW_INSECURE_BACKEND=0
#
# DAINTREE_API_KEY is OPTIONAL and unset on a normal install. When set, the CLI sends it
# as the bearer and the backend spends THAT key instead of its own for your requests. It
# is never prompted for and never written to disk. Kept live for the account sign-in
# being built next.
# DAINTREE_API_KEY=

# ── Daintree MCP connection (injected by Daintree when it launches the CLI) ────────
# Leave unset to run in DEGRADED LOCAL MODE: fs / timer / queue / memory tools work,
# but terminal observation, agent spawning, and every other Daintree orchestration tool
# report a clean "not connected" error. Degraded mode is not a normal launch.
# DAINTREE_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:45454/mcp
# DAINTREE_MCP_TOKEN=...
# DAINTREE_PROJECT_ID=...
# DAINTREE_WINDOW_ID=...

# ── Permissions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tier gates which risk classes are reachable at all:
#   supervisor  read / local / ui
#   operator    + terminal / project / external
#   system      + git / system              (default)
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_TIER=system
#
# AUTO_APPROVE removes the interactive confirmation prompt for the main actor — it does
# NOT widen the tier gate, and unattended actors (watcher / timer / workflow / wake)
# still require a scoped automation grant. Leave it OFF unless you are running an
# automated harness; the cockpit shows a persistent warning badge while it is on.
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_AUTO_APPROVE=0

# ── Diagnostics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A full-fidelity local trace (model requests/responses, tool calls with args+results,
# the watcher lifecycle). Secrets are redacted before they are written, but the trace
# still contains your conversation, terminal output, and file excerpts — it is an
# owner-only local artifact (dir 0700, files 0600, pruned after 7 days), not a support
# artifact. Use `daintree-assistant support-bundle` to hand something to a maintainer.
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_DEBUG_LOG=0
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_LOG_DIR=~/.daintree/logs

# ── Other overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_STATE_DIR=~/.daintree/assistant-cli
# DAINTREE_ASSISTANT_OFFLINE=0
# DAINTREE_THEME=dark            # dark | light | ansi | none
#
# Rollout flag for the workflow execution-graph layer. ON by default — the backend
# now carries the matching workflow_state contract. Set to 0 for a backend that
# does not (or to shrink the surface while chasing an unrelated failure). See
# docs/WORKFLOW_INTELLIGENCE.md.
# DAINTREE_WORKFLOW_INTELLIGENCE=0
